From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:52:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] GPU: textures picked by index served in turns (fork
 #1246; local: OFF by default)

Hand port of fork #1246 (faf709b5): TextureQueue::due serves slots
looked at before and slots never looked at in turns, and a slot whose
memory is not mapped is looked at again after VICTORY_RELOOK_MS.

Local change against the fork: both are OFF unless asked for, so a run
without switches behaves as before this commit.
- VICTORY_FAIR_DUE=1 turns the turns on (the fork: on unless =0). Always
  on in unit tests, which check the order.
- VICTORY_RELOOK_MS unset keeps 4,000 ms and at most 256 slots a pass
  (the fork: 20,000 and 1,024); set, it is used with the fork's 1,024.
The fork's setting is VICTORY_FAIR_DUE=1 VICTORY_RELOOK_MS=20000.

One conflict in descriptor/host.rs (the Mips type next to fair_due).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit faf709b5ea97c72c76905a008d72fee737cde4be, changed)
